%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%%%%%% BIBLIOGRAPHY CATEGORIES %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% The bibliography is printed by category: first the entries of no category,        %
% then each category in the order below, under its heading.  Each category          %
% gets a biblatex filter "mypackage/<category>" (and "mypackage/none" for the       %
% rest).  The entry types are the ones biblatex sees; biber's aliases               %
% (phdthesis, techreport, www, ...) are listed too, for the sort key below.         %
%                                                                                   %
% Numbers: biber numbers the entries in sorting order.  A source map gives every    %
% entry a "presort" value (mp00 for no category, mp01, mp02, ... in the order of    %
% the categories), the first sort key of biblatex's sorting schemes: the numbers    %
% then follow the printed order, without biblatex's "defernumbers" option (which    %
% needed one more LaTeX run).  A presort value given in the .bib file is kept.      %
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\ExplSyntaxOn
